{"uid":"5f431b7f430042ab","name":"TC-417: manual table hold — too early 409, held table annotated not blocked-state, refuses another booking even for a MANAGER, keep stamps, release clears","fullName":"06-reservations-lifecycle.spec.ts:1035:7","historyId":"336db4216ebc74fccb9c3f9767c2e2ae:7e298e2e617906361415d870ccc12df9","time":{"start":1794984582513,"stop":1794984584333,"duration":1820},"description":"Replaces the retired RESERVED_SOON floor state (2026-10-12): a booking never blocks a table on its own; a host HOLDS one by hand via POST /reservations/:id/tables. A booking ~3h out is outside the default 30-min hold window → 409 RESERVATION_HOLD_TOO_EARLY. A booking ~20 min out holds the table: the floor row stays AVAILABLE and carries the `reservedSoon` annotation (the holder). Seating a DIFFERENT booking there → 409 TABLE_HELD even as the MANAGER (a hold is not overridable). `keep` stamps holdKeptAt; `tableIds: []` releases and the annotation disappears.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Replaces the retired RESERVED_SOON floor state (2026-10-12): a booking never blocks a table on its own; a host HOLDS one by hand via POST /reservations/:id/tables. A booking ~3h out is outside the default 30-min hold window → 409 RESERVATION_HOLD_TOO_EARLY. A booking ~20 min out holds the table: the floor row stays AVAILABLE and carries the <code>reservedSoon</code> annotation (the holder). Seating a DIFFERENT booking there → 409 TABLE_HELD even as the MANAGER (a hold is not overridable). <code>keep</code> stamps holdKeptAt; <code>tableIds: []</code> releases and the annotation disappears.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[],"testStage":{"description":"Replaces the retired RESERVED_SOON floor state (2026-10-12): a booking never blocks a table on its own; a host HOLDS one by hand via POST /reservations/:id/tables. A booking ~3h out is outside the default 30-min hold window →